1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:00:46,672 --> 00:00:48,882
EPISODE 11

7
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:51,343
[Sejin] I'm so full I'm going to burst.

8
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,595
[Taeho] Did you eat a lot?

9
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,932
-Oh, right.
-Here are your beers.

10
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,892
[Taeho] Thank you.

11
00:00:58,976 --> 00:01:00,310
[straining] Wait a second.

12
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:02,813
You can give those here.

13
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,398
Here's a glass.

14
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:06,108
-All right.
-Yeah, here.

15
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:07,484
Could you please take these?

16
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:11,113
-Can I have one?
-Let me take the one in there.

17
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:12,823
I'm going to finish Youjin's too.

18
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:14,908
Are we all good?

19
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,662
By the way, where did Minjae go?

20
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,497
-He wasn't in the bathroom.
-He wasn't?

21
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:23,250
It seemed like
he was seeing Lim Youjin off.

22
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:27,462
Hmm. Well, then go tell him to hurry back.

23
00:01:27,546 --> 00:01:29,631
Beer doesn't taste good when it gets warm.

24
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:33,010
Okay.

25
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:35,304
The beer isn't good.

26
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:36,930
-Oh, boy.
-This idiot is drunk.

27
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,600
-He left his beer behind.
-See you in a bit.

28
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,574
Hey. Minjae.

29
00:02:06,043 --> 00:02:07,127
-Hey.
-Hey.

30
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:11,006
Is Youjin gone?

31
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:13,467
Yeah, she's gone.

32
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:19,723
Taeho says you should hurry back
before the beer gets warm.

33
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:22,809
[Minjae] Okay. Let's go.

34
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:45,248
[Youjin] <i>It looks like</i>
<i>I'll be a little late. I'm sorry.</i>

35
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:49,419
[Jihoon] <i>Okay. Call me when you get here.</i>

36
00:02:51,004 --> 00:02:52,214
<i>Where are you now?</i>

37
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:54,299
<i>Call me when you're here.</i>

38
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:57,427
<i>Are you going to be really late?</i>

39
00:02:58,679 --> 00:02:59,680
<i>Where are you?</i>

40
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,057
<i>I'm hungry.</i>

41
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:04,810
<i>Hurry up.</i>

42
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:12,025
CALL ME...

43
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:20,909
Let me refill your glass.

44
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:22,035
Okay. Thank you.

45
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:28,834
Excuse me, sir.

46
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:30,752
Just so you know,

47
00:03:30,836 --> 00:03:33,588
we stop taking food orders at 8:30.

48
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:34,673
Oh...

49
00:03:36,591 --> 00:03:38,718
But it's fine if you're not ordering food.

50
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:41,430
Would you like to see the wine list?

51
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,016
No, I'll order food.

52
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:47,269
-Sure. Let me know when you're ready.
-Okay.

53
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:03,577
POWER OFF

54
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:14,880
So you're saying you'll have
to start your own lab and all that?

55
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,089
Yeah, I will.

56
00:04:18,717 --> 00:04:20,510
How many students will you take on?

57
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:22,262
Well, I don't have much of a budget,

58
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:24,556
and the lab is pretty small,
so I'm not sure.

59
00:04:25,891 --> 00:04:27,392
[Taeho] In that case, Minjae,

60
00:04:27,476 --> 00:04:29,394
there are a few undergrads
I've had my eye on.

61
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:31,396
I'll tell them to reach out to you.

62
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:35,108
We can take care of it ourselves.

63
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:36,985
You're leaving for your postdoc anyway.

64
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:38,653
We'll take care of it.

65
00:04:38,737 --> 00:04:41,406
If you have to go,
you have to go. Just go.

66
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:42,949
-Wow.
-He says just go.

67
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:45,494
[scoffs] You little...

68
00:04:46,745 --> 00:04:48,413
Huh? Jeez.

69
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:53,376
You guys are treating me
like some washed-up old man already.

70
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:54,503
How dare you...

71
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:56,755
Hey, forget it. Don't worry about it.

72
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:58,799
You guys just focus on your own lab.

73
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:00,008
I can take care of mine.

74
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:02,219
Come on, Minjae. Jeez.

75
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,012
I won't be away for long. Okay?

76
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:06,223
I'll be back in Korea
in just a year, you know?

77
00:05:07,474 --> 00:05:09,518
Whatever. You go wherever you have to go.

78
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:11,144
We'll talk once you're back.

79
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,313
Hey, order some more beer.

80
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:15,357
What, more beer? You've had enough.

81
00:05:16,358 --> 00:05:17,734
I didn't even drink that much.

82
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:20,695
Hey, just drink mine...
Actually, just order it.

83
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:23,073
Could we get some more beer, please?

84
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:24,950
-How many?
-Wait, hold on.

85
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:28,328
Then, Minjae, should we go somewhere else
for another round?

86
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:30,747
How about the whelk place?

87
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:32,249
That sounds great.

88
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:33,792
We've just had something fried,

89
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,669
-so soju would be refreshing.
-Yeah.

90
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:38,505
Whelk? Is there a whelk place nearby...

91
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:41,049
No, don't bother looking. I know a place.

92
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:42,467
It's right around the corner.

93
00:05:42,551 --> 00:05:46,179
But Chansoo has to take the subway
all the way to Incheon.

94
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:48,932
He'd be pretty tired
if he went for another round.

95
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:50,350
-[Minjae] Yeah.
-What?

96
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,895
And Lee Kangin has a Champions League
match tonight.

97
00:05:53,979 --> 00:05:55,272
-You can't miss that.
-Oh!

98
00:05:55,981 --> 00:05:57,566
What time is the Champions League?

99
00:05:57,649 --> 00:05:58,859
Around 3 or so.

100
00:05:58,942 --> 00:06:00,902
Yeah. Just go home and watch that.

101
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:02,654
Let's go now. Come on, get up.

102
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:06,575
[groans] There's no need to travel
all the way back to Incheon, right?

103
00:06:07,409 --> 00:06:09,244
We can just watch it at Sejin's.

104
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:10,662
-[Hangyeol] Right.
-What?

105
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:14,457
I mean, we can just get the whelks
and some other food to go, right?

106
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,710
Then have another round
at your place. Okay?

107
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:18,670
And we can all watch the game together,

108
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:22,799
and then all head to work together
tomorrow afternoon.

109
00:06:22,883 --> 00:06:24,092
-[Chansoo] Sounds great.
-[Taeho] Yeah.

110
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:25,594
-[Chansoo] I'd love that.
-[Hangyeol] Sounds perfect.

111
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:28,263
[Minjae] Drink and watch the game
all night, then go to work?

112
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:29,347
Yeah. Why?

113
00:06:29,431 --> 00:06:30,891
Aren't you going to be tired?

114
00:06:30,974 --> 00:06:32,392
[Taeho] Why would I be tired?

115
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:35,186
And I'm the leader of this lab.
If I say we do it, we do it.

116
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:36,563
You don't get a say, okay?

117
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,064
Have it your way.

118
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:39,316
[Taeho grunts] Hmm.

119
00:06:39,858 --> 00:06:44,112
So we'll get the whelks to go
and pick up drinks at a convenience store.

120
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,864
-[Taeho] Yeah, soju's cheaper there.
-[Chansoo] Right.

121
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:50,910
No. The thing is, my home isn't
particularly ready for guests right now.

122
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:53,788
Why not?

123
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:55,290
My place...

124
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:57,876
It's really drafty.

125
00:06:57,959 --> 00:06:59,294
Cold air just comes right in.

126
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:01,087
I'm fine because I'm used to it,

127
00:07:01,171 --> 00:07:05,216
but you guys will freeze
and end up getting sick or something.

128
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,801
You've got heat, damn it.

129
00:07:06,885 --> 00:07:09,971
Just crank it up! Get the place
nice and warm. Don't be cheap.

130
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:11,097
I'm not being cheap.

131
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,432
Jeez.

132
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:17,937
I'm saying, because of the windows,
no matter how I...

133
00:07:18,021 --> 00:07:19,939
Anyway, it just won't work.

134
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:22,484
It's just too cold.
You'll freeze to death.

135
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:25,070
If it's cold, we can just
get under some blankets.

136
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,447
Watching the game together
will be so much fun.

137
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:30,450
Yeah. All right, so this...

138
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:33,203
this is our last drink here.

139
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:35,205
-Let's finish this and get going.
-Okay.

140
00:07:36,373 --> 00:07:38,166
Then how about...

141
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:39,834
[Taeho] Yeah.

142
00:07:40,335 --> 00:07:41,670
Minjae's place?

143
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:42,962
[Minjae] What?

144
00:07:43,046 --> 00:07:44,089
My place?

145
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:46,633
Your new apartment.
It's in Seocho-dong, right?

146
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:47,717
What?

147
00:07:48,385 --> 00:07:50,929
Dream Sun Palace in Seocho-dong.

148
00:07:52,514 --> 00:07:54,391
-And it's on the 33rd floor.
-Thirty...

149
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,643
The view from up there
must be amazing at night.

150
00:07:58,645 --> 00:08:01,439
We can't go to Seocho-dong
at this hour. It's too far.

151
00:08:01,523 --> 00:08:04,401
No, Minjae. It'll only take 15, 20 minutes
by taxi at this hour.

152
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:06,486
[Minjae] The taxi
is going to cost too much. Forget it.

153
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,488
He's got at least two bathrooms

154
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:13,284
and a living room,
where there's almost definitely a TV.

155
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:15,161
-[Taeho] Of course.
-[Chansoo] Well, it's an apartment.

156
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:16,913
-Of course it's got it.
-Yeah.

157
00:08:16,996 --> 00:08:19,457
[Hangyeol] This can be a welcome-back
and housewarming party.

158
00:08:19,541 --> 00:08:22,836
Yeah. Kill two birds
with one stone, as they say.

159
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:25,672
Yeah. Looks like
we've picked the perfect day.

160
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:29,426
All right, then... Everyone, drink up
what's left in your glass and get up.

161
00:08:29,509 --> 00:08:31,177
-Okay.
-All right. Cheers.

162
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:33,096
-Cheers.
-Cheers. I've finished mine.

163
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:34,848
-Drink this.
-You're not going to?

164
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:36,433
-No, you drink it.
-Give it to me.

165
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:40,687
I've never told you where I live.
How did you know?

166
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:42,147
It was written...

167
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:46,026
on the package we got at the lab.
I saw it there.

168
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:47,360
You're unbelievable.

169
00:08:47,444 --> 00:08:50,989
I looked it up, and apparently,
Seocho-dong isn't that far from campus.

170
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,282
Can I come over often?

171
00:08:55,118 --> 00:08:57,495
Excuse me. Could we
have the leftover chicken to go?

172
00:08:58,705 --> 00:08:59,706
[Taeho] All right.

173
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,546
Sir, may I clear the plate for you?

174
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:08,882
-Yes.
-All right.

175
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:14,471
For dessert, we have coffee.
Would you like some?

176
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,391
No, I'm good.

177
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:20,185
All right.

178
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:53,760
[staff] That will be 51,000 won.
Please insert your card.

179
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,428
Would you like a receipt?

180
00:09:55,512 --> 00:09:56,513
[Jihoon] No, thanks.

181
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:58,223
[staff] You're all set. Thank you.

182
00:10:33,258 --> 00:10:34,467
What are you doing here?

183
00:10:38,555 --> 00:10:40,598
-Sorry, I'm late.
-I said, what are you doing here?

184
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:44,435
I spotted this car on my way over.

185
00:10:45,687 --> 00:10:49,232
I took a closer look,
and it looked like your car.

186
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:50,942
So I was wondering if it was yours...

187
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,903
and I guess it really was yours.

188
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:56,739
This is a parking lot.

189
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:59,993
The restaurant over there
is where you eat.

190
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:03,163
-I'm sorry.
-You already said you're sorry.

191
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:07,333
Well, I was going to call you. But...

192
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,217
You're freezing.

193
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:24,601
Have you eaten?

194
00:11:28,897 --> 00:11:30,440
Why haven't you eaten yet?

195
00:11:34,569 --> 00:11:36,946
It's okay. Skipping a meal won't kill you.

196
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,494
I'm sorry I'm late.

197
00:11:43,578 --> 00:11:45,163
I told you, you already said that.

198
00:11:50,752 --> 00:11:52,045
You're here now.

199
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:57,800
That's all that matters.

200
00:11:59,594 --> 00:12:01,971
How long are we going
to be standing here like this?

201
00:12:02,055 --> 00:12:03,056
[Jihoon] All night.

202
00:12:05,225 --> 00:12:06,768
We'll stay like this all night.

203
00:12:10,647 --> 00:12:11,648
Why?

204
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:15,401
You've got other plans?

205
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:21,658
Have you been crying?

206
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,118
No, I haven't.

207
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,415
<i>-</i>[automated voice]<i> Going down.</i>
-Isn't it here?

208
00:12:29,499 --> 00:12:30,625
Aren't we getting off?

209
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:31,709
Right. It's here.

210
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:34,045
Come this way.

211
00:12:35,505 --> 00:12:37,048
It's so nice here.

212
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:47,100
Jeez.

213
00:12:49,978 --> 00:12:52,480
Coming in. [chuckling]

214
00:12:53,815 --> 00:12:54,816
Coming through.

215
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,734
-Your home.
-Excuse me.

216
00:13:01,072 --> 00:13:02,073
All right.

217
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:04,284
Minjae, how do you turn on the light?

218
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:08,705
-[Chansoo] Where is it?
-[Minjae grunts]

219
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:25,680
I don't think
we can see the Hangang River.

220
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,849
-[Taeho] Right? But the view is nice.
-[Hangyeol] The view is nice.

221
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:30,351
We're in Gangnam, so that makes sense.

222
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:32,312
-We're facing away from it.
-That's right.

223
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:33,896
This is...

224
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,315
[Minjae] Guys, wash your hands first.

225
00:13:35,398 --> 00:13:37,275
[Sejin] Excuse me.
I'll use the bathroom.

226
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:44,073
[Taeho] This is a walk-in closet.

227
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:45,241
[Chansoo] I can't see anything.

228
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:47,035
-There's nothing.
-Minjae, one second.

229
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,708
[Chansoo] Hangyeol.

230
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:55,460
Hangyeol, what are you trying on?

231
00:13:58,337 --> 00:13:59,881
[Taeho] It looks pretty good on you.

232
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:01,799
-[Hangyeol] Minjae.
-Yeah?

233
00:14:01,883 --> 00:14:03,843
I've never seen you wear this hat.

234
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,345
If you don't wear it, can I have it?

235
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:10,058
I wear it. Put it back.
Come on, put it back.

236
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:12,101
-But I've never seen you wear it.
-I do.

237
00:14:13,311 --> 00:14:15,438
-Minjae, how about this one?
-[Minjae] What?

238
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:16,773
Do you wear this too?

239
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:17,857
I do... [groans softly]

240
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:20,276
I do. Come on, put it back...

241
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:22,487
What are you doing?
Just come sit down already!

242
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:24,655
-[Taeho] What'd you think of this one?
-[Chansoo] It's nice.

243
00:14:24,739 --> 00:14:27,075
-[Hangyeol] What's that?
-[Taeho] Obviously, it's Minjae's.

244
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,367
-[laughing]
-[Chansoo] It's Minjae's?

245
00:14:28,451 --> 00:14:29,535
-[Taeho] Yeah.
-[Hangyeol] This one?

246
00:14:29,619 --> 00:14:31,037
Hey, he's going to get mad at you.

247
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,205
[Taeho] It's okay.

248
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:33,915
God damn it.

249
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:35,833
[Taeho] Hey, Hangyeol, you...

250
00:14:35,917 --> 00:14:38,127
Those pants are pretty nice. Yeah.

251
00:14:38,211 --> 00:14:40,046
-[Chansoo] You're wearing his pants?
-Damn it.

252
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:42,715
[Taeho] Well, he's also...

253
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:44,759
He's pretty tall,
so he pulls it off nicely.

254
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:47,386
-[continues indistinctly]
-[sighs] God damn it. For God's sake.

255
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:11,327
[Taeho laughing] You can't pull it off.

256
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:13,204
-[Chansoo] Come on, why?
-[laughter continues]

257
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:24,048
Damn it.

258
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:10,655
[Jihoon] Try it.

259
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,990
You said you liked it the other day.

260
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:19,914
Do you want something else?
Should I order something else?

261
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,877
Do you want to go home?
Should I take you home?

262
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,342
You don't want to go home.

263
00:17:31,425 --> 00:17:33,511
Do you want to go somewhere else instead?

264
00:17:36,556 --> 00:17:37,557
Hmm?

265
00:17:42,103 --> 00:17:43,896
Tell me. What do you want to eat?

266
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:47,817
I just don't want to eat anything.

267
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,235
I can't get anything down.

268
00:17:52,655 --> 00:17:54,407
-Professor.
-Yes.

269
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:58,411
We had some abalone left over today,
so I made some abalone porridge.

270
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:02,540
Abalone porridge would be great.
Thank you, sir.

271
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:05,418
-Sure.
-No, I'm okay. I can just eat this.

272
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:10,047
-We'll have the porridge, please.
-[staff] Okay.

273
00:18:12,008 --> 00:18:13,050
-Thank you.
-Sure.

274
00:18:14,302 --> 00:18:16,137
But I don't want abalone porridge.

275
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:18,889
Why come if you'll just say no
to everything?

276
00:18:18,973 --> 00:18:20,266
Just to give me a hard time?

277
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:24,478
Well, because you asked me to come out...

278
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:33,821
You said you got me a gift. Give it to me.

279
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:35,239
I didn't. There's nothing.

280
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:57,011
I'll give it to you
if you eat the abalone porridge.

281
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,273
Can I open it?

282
00:19:33,631 --> 00:19:34,799
Do you want to try it on?

283
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:36,592
Well...

284
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:44,141
What's wrong? You don't like it?

285
00:19:44,225 --> 00:19:45,893
No, that's not it.

286
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:48,938
-It seems too expensive, so...
-It's not that expensive.

287
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:54,193
It's too much. I don't think
I can accept it. I'm sorry.

288
00:19:59,532 --> 00:20:00,950
But I bought it for you.

289
00:20:05,079 --> 00:20:06,455
I bought it for you.

290
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:07,581
I don't want it.

291
00:20:11,502 --> 00:20:13,754
People who don't know
might get the wrong idea,

292
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:18,259
and I don't want any weird rumors
to start about you because of me.

293
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:19,343
I don't want that.

294
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:21,762
What rumors?

295
00:20:23,514 --> 00:20:25,474
About us seeing each other or something.

296
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:27,476
Apparently, some students are saying that.

297
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:31,981
You know how some people at school
spread weird rumors like that.

298
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:36,485
I don't care.

299
00:20:37,987 --> 00:20:38,988
Pardon?

300
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,991
The rumors and the people
talking about it.

301
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:45,411
I'm not afraid of any of that,
and I don't care.

302
00:20:46,537 --> 00:20:47,538
Well, but--

303
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:49,665
Giving pretty things to the woman I like

304
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:53,210
and making her happy.

305
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,088
That's enough for me.

306
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:06,223
But I already like someone.

307
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:12,062
I already like someone.

308
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:19,528
Okay.

309
00:21:23,741 --> 00:21:25,326
So keep liking him.

310
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:27,161
What?

311
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:30,080
You can keep liking him. It's okay.

312
00:21:34,585 --> 00:21:35,753
But I...

313
00:21:37,505 --> 00:21:40,090
can't reciprocate your feelings.

314
00:21:41,175 --> 00:21:44,094
What matters is
that I gave you my whole heart.

315
00:21:44,178 --> 00:21:46,263
Who cares if it's not reciprocated?

316
00:21:46,347 --> 00:21:48,098
We don't have to keep score like this.

317
00:21:52,478 --> 00:21:53,896
So, Youjin, you should...

318
00:21:56,357 --> 00:21:58,359
Why do you make yourself suffer so much?

319
00:21:59,944 --> 00:22:02,696
You think his feelings for you
aren't as deep as yours,

320
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:06,075
and you resent him for it,
like you've somehow lost out.

321
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:07,368
You don't have to do that.

322
00:22:08,118 --> 00:22:11,205
-That's not what it is.
-That's exactly what it is. I'm right.

323
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:17,086
Who said I wanted him
to feel exactly the same way I do,

324
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:19,922
as if our feelings
were balanced on scales?

325
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,215
That's not what I mean.

326
00:22:22,883 --> 00:22:25,719
I gave him my whole heart, my everything.

327
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:29,723
But he betrayed it all
and just threw it away.

328
00:22:30,975 --> 00:22:31,976
He's a traitor.

329
00:22:34,979 --> 00:22:37,940
And it put me through so much pain,
I felt like I could die.

330
00:22:43,237 --> 00:22:44,905
That's what love does.

331
00:22:46,824 --> 00:22:49,118
It leaves you a complete train wreck.

332
00:22:51,245 --> 00:22:54,957
A train wreck is someone who's
completely wrecked, like a derailed train.

333
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,293
That's what loving someone can do to you.

334
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:03,591
You give them the power
to wreck your heart at any moment.

335
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:08,012
I don't want to give anyone that power.

336
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:09,221
Even if you don't,

337
00:23:10,723 --> 00:23:13,475
you can't just take the good stuff
and skip the bad.

338
00:23:13,559 --> 00:23:16,520
They're two sides of the same coin.
It's just the way it is.

339
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:25,946
Otherwise, it's not love.
It's all fake and a lie.

340
00:23:30,993 --> 00:23:32,786
So stop being stubborn

341
00:23:33,996 --> 00:23:35,539
and just keep liking him

342
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:38,250
as much as you want,

343
00:23:38,334 --> 00:23:39,752
as much as you can.

344
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:45,424
Keep liking him.

345
00:23:47,217 --> 00:23:49,303
Until those feelings wear themselves out.

346
00:25:35,659 --> 00:25:39,038
MOVE TO TRASH

347
00:25:40,789 --> 00:25:41,832
CANCEL

348
00:26:56,782 --> 00:27:01,370
MOVE TO TRASH

349
00:27:05,916 --> 00:27:07,793
MOVE TO TRASH

350
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:12,459
Looks like he doesn't have any big plates.

351
00:29:12,542 --> 00:29:16,004
Forget it. Just bring the whole pan here.

352
00:29:17,172 --> 00:29:18,173
Okay.

353
00:29:33,981 --> 00:29:35,983
Jeez.

354
00:29:39,611 --> 00:29:40,946
Hey, Kim Sejin.

355
00:29:41,613 --> 00:29:43,699
Go tell the guys to come and eat.

356
00:29:46,118 --> 00:29:47,119
Okay.

357
00:29:49,413 --> 00:29:52,082
Chansoo. Hangyeol.

358
00:29:53,583 --> 00:29:55,168
He says come eat the <i>pajeon</i> first.

359
00:29:55,252 --> 00:29:56,837
-Right. Okay.
-We'll be right out.

360
00:29:56,962 --> 00:29:59,006
-After this round.
-We'll be right there.

361
00:29:59,673 --> 00:30:00,924
-[Chansoo] Damn it.
-[Hangyeol]There you go.

362
00:30:01,717 --> 00:30:02,968
[Chansoo] What's wrong with this?

363
00:30:03,051 --> 00:30:04,219
[Sejin] Hurry up.

364
00:30:05,345 --> 00:30:07,055
They say they'll be right here.

365
00:30:07,139 --> 00:30:09,558
Okay. Go get Minjae too.

366
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:11,977
Tell him to come out and eat with us.

367
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:13,979
I think he's asleep.

368
00:30:14,062 --> 00:30:15,731
Then wake him up. [clicks tongue]

369
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:18,400
Tell him the game starts soon,
so he should come quickly.

370
00:30:19,901 --> 00:30:21,737
[clicks tongue] Come on!

371
00:30:26,324 --> 00:30:27,325
Jeez.

372
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:32,622
Minjae, are you asleep?

373
00:30:34,207 --> 00:30:35,834
Come out and have some <i>pajeon.</i>

374
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:48,138
Hey, Chansoo, Hangyeol, come on out!

375
00:30:48,221 --> 00:30:50,640
Minjae, are you okay?

376
00:30:50,724 --> 00:30:54,436
Yeah, I'm okay.

377
00:30:59,399 --> 00:31:01,318
Wait, careful. Wait.

378
00:31:04,571 --> 00:31:07,532
Careful. Be careful. Oh, boy.

379
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:13,121
-It's okay.
-[gags]

380
00:31:20,212 --> 00:31:23,090
[Sejin] Minjae, are you okay?

381
00:31:23,173 --> 00:31:25,675
Do you want me to get you
some stomach medicine?

382
00:31:25,759 --> 00:31:27,219
[Minjae] No, I'm fine.

383
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:28,595
Go. I'm fine.

384
00:31:39,189 --> 00:31:40,190
Oh, man.

385
00:31:46,029 --> 00:31:48,240
What's up? He doesn't want to come out?

386
00:31:48,323 --> 00:31:49,449
No.

387
00:31:49,991 --> 00:31:51,910
It looks like he's feeling sick.

388
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:53,745
I don't think he's going to eat this.

389
00:31:54,371 --> 00:31:56,123
Why? Why is he feeling sick?

390
00:31:58,542 --> 00:31:59,876
Could it be indigestion?

391
00:32:00,669 --> 00:32:02,587
He barely drank anything, though.

392
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:05,757
Not sure. I think
he has a bit of a fever, too.

393
00:32:05,841 --> 00:32:07,425
Maybe it's a cold.

394
00:32:07,509 --> 00:32:10,262
Well, he was busy
with the move and everything.

395
00:32:10,345 --> 00:32:11,596
That must be why he's sick.

396
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:15,267
I wonder if any pharmacies
are still open this late.

397
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:17,686
Hey, if the pharmacies are closed,

398
00:32:17,769 --> 00:32:20,021
you can get cold medicine
at convenience stores...

399
00:32:22,524 --> 00:32:24,776
Hey, Sejin. Wait, you...

400
00:32:26,194 --> 00:32:27,279
Hey, this...

401
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:28,446
What's this?

402
00:32:29,197 --> 00:32:31,408
It must be from
when Minjae threw up earlier.

403
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:32,492
[Taeho] What the...

404
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:37,455
Hey, call 119. Now!

405
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:39,833
[Chansoo] Wait, why? What's wrong?

406
00:32:39,916 --> 00:32:41,209
-What's up?
-[Taeho] Hey, Minjae.

407
00:32:41,293 --> 00:32:42,294
[Chansoo] I don't know.

408
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:46,214
Hey. Open your eyes. Hey. Minjae!

409
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:47,382
[Hangyeol]Minjae, what's up?

410
00:32:48,383 --> 00:32:49,384
My phone!

411
00:33:20,999 --> 00:33:27,088
RESTRICTED AREA

412
00:33:31,259 --> 00:33:34,387
A patient named Park Minjae
was brought in a little while ago.

413
00:33:34,471 --> 00:33:35,680
Where is he?

414
00:33:35,764 --> 00:33:37,724
-He was throwing up blood.
-[telephone ringing]

415
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:38,808
Excuse me.

416
00:33:39,643 --> 00:33:41,686
Hello, this is Nurse Jo Geonu in the ER.

417
00:33:42,979 --> 00:33:43,980
Yes.

418
00:33:45,106 --> 00:33:46,983
The MRI scan's just finished?

419
00:33:48,401 --> 00:33:50,195
-I'm kind of tied up here.
-Yeah, Taeho.

420
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:52,656
We just got to the ER. Where are you?

421
00:33:54,991 --> 00:33:56,326
-Taeho.
-Hey.

422
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,371
I said you didn't need to come.
Why did you come?

423
00:33:59,454 --> 00:34:00,538
Where's Minjae?

424
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:02,749
He just went in for a test.

425
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:06,670
But why did he throw up blood
all of a sudden?

426
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:09,714
I don't know. I guess the test will tell.

427
00:34:09,798 --> 00:34:12,425
It's not life-threatening
or anything, right?

428
00:34:12,509 --> 00:34:14,219
Dude, don't freaking jinx it.

429
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:17,472
He's fine. It's not a big deal.

430
00:34:17,555 --> 00:34:19,266
It's probably not a big deal.

431
00:34:19,349 --> 00:34:20,392
Yeah.

432
00:34:21,518 --> 00:34:23,853
It's not a big deal,
and we're just overreacting.

433
00:34:23,937 --> 00:34:24,938
Taeho is right.

434
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:27,941
Not really. Minjae has cancer.

435
00:34:30,235 --> 00:34:33,405
I heard he had surgery

436
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:35,824
and went through chemo in Canada.

437
00:34:36,283 --> 00:34:37,284
Huh?

438
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:41,746
Shouldn't we call his house, too?

439
00:34:43,248 --> 00:34:45,750
But there's no one there.

440
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:00,515
Jeez, this place...

441
00:35:09,024 --> 00:35:10,025
What?

442
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:11,693
Oh, my goodness.

443
00:35:11,776 --> 00:35:13,612
Why is it so messy here?

444
00:35:15,363 --> 00:35:16,573
Park Minjae!

445
00:35:17,616 --> 00:35:20,327
Come on out. Minjae.

446
00:35:22,329 --> 00:35:23,330
Huh?

447
00:35:33,465 --> 00:35:34,716
My goodness.

448
00:35:55,111 --> 00:35:57,155
Jeez. Seriously.

449
00:35:59,574 --> 00:36:03,119
Where on earth did he go
even without his phone?

450
00:36:04,746 --> 00:36:07,207
And he left the whole place
a complete mess.

451
00:36:08,375 --> 00:36:10,960
You're in big trouble
when you get home, young man.

452
00:36:11,044 --> 00:36:12,671
Unbelievable.

453
00:36:13,963 --> 00:36:16,299
And what's all this on the table...

454
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:21,763
What's this?

455
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:40,615
-[footsteps approaching]
-[door slams]

456
00:36:43,410 --> 00:36:44,786
Yes, hello? [panting]

457
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:46,538
[Jaehong] <i>Hi. Who's this?</i>

458
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:48,790
<i>It's not Sejin this time.</i>
<i>It's you, Youjin.</i>

459
00:36:49,499 --> 00:36:51,209
Where did Sejin go?

460
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:52,585
Kim Sejin?

461
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:57,048
Uh, Sejin went to the restroom.

462
00:36:57,799 --> 00:36:59,801
Yeah, that's why I picked up.

463
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:03,471
I see. Then...
Chansoo came in today, right?

464
00:37:03,555 --> 00:37:07,308
Chansoo? Yes. He did. He came in.

465
00:37:07,392 --> 00:37:09,894
[Jaehong] <i>Well, you know that experiment</i>
<i>from last week?</i>

466
00:37:09,978 --> 00:37:12,063
I wanted to ask him
to bring the data up here.

467
00:37:13,148 --> 00:37:14,315
Yes, right now.

468
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:19,070
He's not there?

469
00:37:19,154 --> 00:37:23,032
No. I mean, he came in, and he was here
until just a little while ago,

470
00:37:24,367 --> 00:37:28,079
but a meeting with an outside visitor
suddenly came up.

471
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,998
Yeah. So he stepped out for a bit.

472
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:32,292
An outside visitor?
An outside visitor who?

473
00:37:32,375 --> 00:37:34,294
No, nothing like that was on the schedule.

474
00:37:34,377 --> 00:37:37,172
Uh... I'm not sure who it is.

475
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:41,092
Well, it came up all of a sudden,
so he had to rush out,

476
00:37:41,176 --> 00:37:43,136
which is why he didn't
tell you beforehand.

477
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:44,220
[Jaehong] <i>He rushed out?</i>

478
00:37:44,304 --> 00:37:46,181
Where? Why would he rush out?

479
00:37:47,348 --> 00:37:49,184
Did you guys get in trouble again?

480
00:37:49,934 --> 00:37:52,771
Put Taeho... Put Taeho on the phone.
Come on, hurry.

481
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:55,732
<i>Taeho is not at his desk right now.</i>

482
00:37:56,608 --> 00:37:59,652
He just went to a nearby...

483
00:38:00,653 --> 00:38:03,490
[sighs] ...restroom. Yeah.

484
00:38:05,158 --> 00:38:08,536
He went to a nearby restroom?

485
00:38:10,997 --> 00:38:11,998
All right.

486
00:38:25,804 --> 00:38:28,264
Look at the time.
And four of you still aren't here?

487
00:38:30,099 --> 00:38:31,935
I guess I've been too easy on you.

488
00:38:32,018 --> 00:38:35,355
You know there's nothing I hate more
than people being late, right?

489
00:38:36,356 --> 00:38:37,357
Yes.

490
00:38:38,483 --> 00:38:43,738
Have I ever nagged you even once

491
00:38:44,781 --> 00:38:49,244
about your research performance
or how your experiments are going?

492
00:38:50,954 --> 00:38:52,497
No, right?

493
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:55,792
All I ask is that you show up on time,
answer the phone politely...

494
00:38:55,875 --> 00:38:57,836
[yelling] ...and don't lie to me!

495
00:38:59,462 --> 00:39:03,633
Haven't I told you many times
that's all I ask?

496
00:39:05,426 --> 00:39:06,469
Yes, you have.

497
00:39:08,388 --> 00:39:11,432
These lazy, idle bastards...

498
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:13,852
are all dead today.

499
00:39:15,645 --> 00:39:18,106
This is my fault. It's on me.

500
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:23,444
-Put that down. Put it down.
-What?

501
00:39:23,528 --> 00:39:24,529
Don't.

502
00:39:25,697 --> 00:39:26,990
For every minute they're late,

503
00:39:27,073 --> 00:39:29,409
-they're getting one whack with the bat.
-[phone vibrating]

504
00:39:32,287 --> 00:39:34,455
And Taeho, who's supposed
to be the lab lead,

505
00:39:34,539 --> 00:39:35,707
deserves it the most.

506
00:39:36,666 --> 00:39:39,377
So instead of getting your ass
over here right now,

507
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:41,796
you have the nerve
to call your professor, you punk?

508
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:44,632
You! Have you lost your damn mind?

509
00:39:45,967 --> 00:39:47,969
What do you mean, listen?

510
00:39:49,637 --> 00:39:51,055
Which hospital?

511
00:39:54,058 --> 00:39:55,935
Seohan National University Hospital? Why?

512
00:39:59,272 --> 00:40:00,273
Yeah.

513
00:40:03,109 --> 00:40:04,110
Yeah, and?

514
00:40:06,446 --> 00:40:09,324
Yeah. Minjae threw up blood?

515
00:40:11,868 --> 00:40:15,663
I mean, throwing up blood means...
he actually vomited blood, right?

516
00:40:17,999 --> 00:40:20,543
Okay, he needs surgery. Okay.

517
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:25,256
A procedure? What's the difference
between surgery and a procedure?

518
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:26,841
Yeah.

519
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:33,431
[sighs] It's lucky you guys happened
to be there with him.

520
00:40:34,807 --> 00:40:38,186
Yeah. Imagine if he'd been home alone.
That could've been really bad.

521
00:40:39,020 --> 00:40:40,313
Talk about a stroke of luck.

522
00:40:40,396 --> 00:40:42,023
Why? Who had surgery?

523
00:40:43,399 --> 00:40:46,694
Well, Youjin is here,
so don't worry about us here.

524
00:40:46,778 --> 00:40:49,697
Yeah, I guess you guys
should stay there then.

525
00:40:49,781 --> 00:40:52,450
Yeah. I'm sure
it's hectic over there, so...

526
00:40:52,533 --> 00:40:54,035
All right. Bye.

527
00:40:56,204 --> 00:40:58,247
What happened? Who had surgery?

528
00:40:58,331 --> 00:41:00,291
[sighs] Apparently,

529
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:03,002
Minjae threw up blood last night.

530
00:41:05,421 --> 00:41:08,174
Well, he's not
in a really serious condition or anything.

531
00:41:09,175 --> 00:41:11,511
They say he needs some kind
of surgery or procedure.

532
00:41:13,846 --> 00:41:15,890
Yeah. Well, it's nothing major, though.

533
00:41:15,974 --> 00:41:18,685
They say it's a simple procedure
to stop the bleeding,

534
00:41:18,768 --> 00:41:20,144
so we shouldn't worry.

535
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:22,146
-Okay.
-Yeah.

536
00:41:22,897 --> 00:41:26,651
Anyway, looks like
you'll have to work by yourself today.

537
00:41:27,694 --> 00:41:28,778
-Okay.
-Yeah.

538
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:32,865
From now on, just tell me the truth.

539
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:34,993
See you later.

540
00:41:49,549 --> 00:41:53,428
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

541
00:42:07,608 --> 00:42:10,445
Hi, I'm the guardian
of patient Park Minjae.

542
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:12,155
One moment, please.

543
00:42:13,781 --> 00:42:15,783
What's your relationship to the patient?

544
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:18,828
I'm his mother.

545
00:42:42,477 --> 00:42:44,187
-[knocking at door]
-[door sliding]

546
00:42:45,855 --> 00:42:47,190
What...

547
00:42:49,901 --> 00:42:51,110
Oh, my gosh.

548
00:42:51,194 --> 00:42:53,279
You can't sleep in this bed.

549
00:42:55,740 --> 00:42:56,741
Sorry.

550
00:42:57,992 --> 00:43:00,119
Who is Mr. Park Minjae's guardian?

551
00:43:00,203 --> 00:43:01,204
Right, it's me.

552
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:04,207
No, I'm Park Minjae's guardian. [grunts]

553
00:43:09,545 --> 00:43:13,007
So it was his mother back then.

554
00:43:15,968 --> 00:43:17,887
That was definitely my mistake.

555
00:43:22,809 --> 00:43:24,268
GASTROENTEROLOGIST JEONG YEONGJU

556
00:43:24,352 --> 00:43:27,647
We performed an emergency endoscopy
and ligated the bleeding vessel.

557
00:43:27,730 --> 00:43:30,858
Uh, the bleeding has been
successfully controlled.

558
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:34,779
We'd like to keep him in the hospital
and monitor him for any further bleeding.

559
00:43:35,905 --> 00:43:38,282
What about his fever
and inflammatory markers?

560
00:43:38,366 --> 00:43:43,121
The fever and sore throat he has
are just symptoms of a mild cold.

561
00:43:43,204 --> 00:43:45,081
It's nothing to be too concerned about.

562
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:47,708
So he's okay?

563
00:43:47,792 --> 00:43:53,422
[chuckles softly] Severe bleeding
like this can lead to shock or even death,

564
00:43:53,506 --> 00:43:56,384
so it was lucky his friends
got him to the hospital quickly.

565
00:43:56,467 --> 00:43:58,678
But all that bleeding out of nowhere...

566
00:43:59,595 --> 00:44:04,934
Could it be some kind of complication
from his recent lung tumor surgery?

567
00:44:05,017 --> 00:44:06,686
Maybe something that's come back or...

568
00:44:06,769 --> 00:44:08,980
Hmm... It has nothing to do
with his lungs.

569
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:11,732
According to the endoscopy,

570
00:44:11,816 --> 00:44:15,778
the cause of the bleeding
was a pretty big stomach ulcer.

571
00:44:15,862 --> 00:44:18,364
So he lost a lot of blood,
and it was pretty serious.

572
00:44:18,447 --> 00:44:20,825
Why would he suddenly
develop a stomach ulcer?

573
00:44:20,908 --> 00:44:24,245
Well, it's hard
to pinpoint the exact cause,

574
00:44:24,328 --> 00:44:27,248
but peptic ulcers are common
in people under a lot of stress,

575
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:29,834
people who've been
taking painkillers for a long time,

576
00:44:29,917 --> 00:44:32,170
and people who drink or smoke a lot.

577
00:44:33,337 --> 00:44:38,134
He needs to avoid stress,
and absolutely no drinking or smoking.

578
00:44:39,302 --> 00:44:42,096
I see. Thank you.

579
00:44:52,356 --> 00:44:53,649
Mr. Kim Gyeongho.

580
00:44:53,733 --> 00:44:54,817
-Yes.
-Come in.

581
00:45:00,448 --> 00:45:01,949
You're not children.

582
00:45:02,617 --> 00:45:06,037
How can you be so immature
and irresponsible? Huh?

583
00:45:07,079 --> 00:45:10,791
You're all smart enough to get PhDs
and even become professors someday.

584
00:45:11,792 --> 00:45:14,921
What's the point of being smart
if you can't get your lives together?

585
00:45:15,713 --> 00:45:18,549
How are you supposed
to teach students someday like this?

586
00:45:22,887 --> 00:45:23,930
And, Taeho,

587
00:45:24,722 --> 00:45:26,515
you really let me down.

588
00:45:27,975 --> 00:45:29,477
You're older than the other kids.

589
00:45:30,978 --> 00:45:32,355
I'm sorry.

590
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:34,690
The other kids might not have known,

591
00:45:34,774 --> 00:45:37,985
but you've known Minjae the longest,
and you're close with him.

592
00:45:38,069 --> 00:45:39,528
You know what he's been through.

593
00:45:40,863 --> 00:45:41,864
I'm sorry.

594
00:45:43,491 --> 00:45:46,285
Why did you have to let him
drink so much when he's sick?

595
00:45:47,328 --> 00:45:49,497
[trembling] I really didn't know, I swear.

596
00:45:49,580 --> 00:45:54,543
I just found out today that he had surgery
and went through chemo in Canada.

597
00:45:56,045 --> 00:46:00,883
Hey, why didn't you tell us
if you knew about it?

598
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:03,010
Well...

599
00:46:03,094 --> 00:46:06,430
Minjae told me not to tell anyone.

600
00:46:06,514 --> 00:46:09,934
Hey, you still should've told us.

601
00:46:10,017 --> 00:46:12,895
Why can't you figure out
what to say and what not to say?

602
00:46:15,231 --> 00:46:18,651
You know what? Somehow,
you never say the things you should

603
00:46:18,734 --> 00:46:20,945
and always say the things you shouldn't.

604
00:46:21,028 --> 00:46:24,907
Right. You said this weird thing
about Minjae and his mother earlier, too.

605
00:46:26,367 --> 00:46:27,827
What weird thing?

606
00:46:28,536 --> 00:46:30,162
No, it's nothing.

607
00:46:30,246 --> 00:46:32,039
What do you mean, nothing?

608
00:46:32,123 --> 00:46:36,502
You saw Minjae and his mother together
and said something weird about them.

609
00:46:36,585 --> 00:46:38,504
And the whole lab went crazy over it.

610
00:46:38,587 --> 00:46:39,839
No.

611
00:46:39,922 --> 00:46:41,674
[Hangyeol] Minjae denied it,

612
00:46:41,757 --> 00:46:45,136
but you didn't believe him
and said she touched him.

613
00:46:45,845 --> 00:46:48,973
You just kept insisting then.

614
00:46:50,141 --> 00:46:51,726
Saw what?

615
00:46:51,809 --> 00:46:53,269
What are you guys talking about?

616
00:46:53,352 --> 00:46:54,353
No.

617
00:46:54,437 --> 00:46:57,565
We can't really tell you what,

618
00:46:57,648 --> 00:46:59,567
but he had the whole lab freak out.

619
00:47:01,944 --> 00:47:06,824
Does this mean Minjae was stressed out
because of you?

620
00:47:06,907 --> 00:47:08,784
No, it wasn't because of me.

621
00:47:09,785 --> 00:47:13,789
Minjae got sick and threw up blood
because of you, man.

622
00:47:23,090 --> 00:47:26,844
That's it. I don't want you
seeing Minjae anymore.

623
00:47:27,887 --> 00:47:28,888
Pardon?

624
00:47:29,805 --> 00:47:32,725
I'll tell Professor Ahn about it.

625
00:47:32,808 --> 00:47:35,811
What? Tell Professor Ahn what...

626
00:47:39,190 --> 00:47:40,733
Wait, Minjae...

627
00:47:41,567 --> 00:47:43,694
didn't throw up blood because of me.

628
00:47:51,035 --> 00:47:52,787
It's all because of Lim Youjin.

629
00:47:52,870 --> 00:47:54,622
[Taeho scoffs] What about Youjin?

630
00:48:00,044 --> 00:48:03,005
Minjae and Lim Youjin
were secretly dating.

631
00:48:05,132 --> 00:48:06,884
They kept it under wraps,

632
00:48:08,844 --> 00:48:11,430
but then they broke up
when Minjae left for the States.

633
00:48:11,514 --> 00:48:15,351
Then when he came back to Korea,
he still wasn't over her

634
00:48:15,434 --> 00:48:17,269
and asked her to get back together.

635
00:48:17,353 --> 00:48:19,146
But she said no.

636
00:48:19,230 --> 00:48:22,608
Because she's seeing someone else now.

637
00:48:26,445 --> 00:48:31,575
That's why Minjae got stressed out,
drank, and threw up blood.

638
00:48:35,996 --> 00:48:37,581
It's all because of Lim Youjin,

639
00:48:39,375 --> 00:48:40,418
not me.

640
00:49:25,421 --> 00:49:28,924
Hello, I'm here to visit a patient
named Park Minjae.

641
00:49:30,342 --> 00:49:33,387
I heard he was taken to the ER last night
and had surgery.

642
00:49:34,722 --> 00:49:35,723
Are you his family?

643
00:49:36,599 --> 00:49:38,934
I'm not his family.
I'm his junior from school.

644
00:49:39,018 --> 00:49:41,312
If you're not family, you can't visit him.

645
00:49:42,897 --> 00:49:45,232
His guardian asked
for him not to have any visitors.

646
00:49:46,901 --> 00:49:47,902
I see.

647
00:49:52,865 --> 00:49:55,910
Then, can he eat something like porridge?

648
00:49:55,993 --> 00:49:57,077
Pardon?

649
00:49:57,161 --> 00:49:58,787
When I had my appendix out,

650
00:49:58,871 --> 00:50:01,624
I could start eating thin rice porridge
after about 3 days.

651
00:50:02,416 --> 00:50:05,336
We can't give out that kind
of information about a patient.

652
00:50:06,670 --> 00:50:08,297
I see. Thank you.

653
00:50:31,362 --> 00:50:33,822
[automated voice]<i> The bus is arriving.</i>

654
00:52:28,479 --> 00:52:32,024
Hello. I'm here to visit a patient
named Park Minjae.

655
00:52:32,941 --> 00:52:35,361
Is he still not allowed to have visitors?

656
00:52:35,444 --> 00:52:39,490
If I can't see him, could you
at least give him this porridge for me?

657
00:52:39,573 --> 00:52:40,824
One moment, please.

658
00:52:44,161 --> 00:52:48,165
Uh, I'm not seeing any record here.

659
00:54:45,324 --> 00:54:46,325
Hey.

660
00:54:46,408 --> 00:54:47,534
Hello.

661
00:54:47,618 --> 00:54:48,619
You're here.

662
00:54:51,497 --> 00:54:52,706
You're here, so come in.

663
00:54:52,789 --> 00:54:55,042
No, I don't need to.

664
00:54:55,125 --> 00:54:57,419
That's some porridge, though.
You should have some.

665
00:54:58,462 --> 00:54:59,463
Oh!

666
00:55:01,131 --> 00:55:02,633
It's for me.

667
00:55:02,716 --> 00:55:04,218
Thanks, I appreciate it.

668
00:55:04,301 --> 00:55:05,302
Sure.

669
00:55:07,179 --> 00:55:09,556
-[elevator dings]
<i>-</i>[automated voice]<i> Going down.</i>

670
00:55:09,640 --> 00:55:11,350
[Minjae] Bye. Have a safe trip home.

671
00:55:22,945 --> 00:55:25,072
Right...

672
00:55:25,155 --> 00:55:26,490
Do you want some juice?

673
00:55:27,032 --> 00:55:28,116
No, I'm fine.

674
00:55:29,117 --> 00:55:32,287
Okay, then let me
make you a cup of hot tea.

675
00:55:32,371 --> 00:55:33,622
I'll just have water.

676
00:55:35,332 --> 00:55:36,625
Right. Okay.

677
00:55:39,002 --> 00:55:40,337
Let's see.

678
00:55:51,056 --> 00:55:52,057
Have a seat.

679
00:55:52,140 --> 00:55:53,141
Okay.

680
00:56:10,867 --> 00:56:12,077
-Hey.
-Hey. Yeah?

681
00:56:12,828 --> 00:56:13,829
Go on.

682
00:56:13,912 --> 00:56:15,664
No, you go first.

683
00:56:16,290 --> 00:56:17,332
Ah.

684
00:56:19,376 --> 00:56:22,212
I was just going to say
I appreciate the porridge.

685
00:56:23,589 --> 00:56:24,590
Oh...

686
00:56:27,593 --> 00:56:29,511
How are you doing after the surgery?

687
00:56:29,595 --> 00:56:30,804
Oh, that.

688
00:56:31,763 --> 00:56:34,141
I ended up with a hole
in my stomach from drinking.

689
00:56:34,224 --> 00:56:35,934
Patching it up isn't even surgery.

690
00:56:38,228 --> 00:56:40,230
I'm supposed to be your senior.

691
00:56:40,314 --> 00:56:41,773
This is pretty embarrassing.

692
00:56:44,693 --> 00:56:46,486
But you shouldn't push yourself.

693
00:56:48,447 --> 00:56:50,741
Do you want me to help you
with the unpacking?

694
00:56:51,867 --> 00:56:53,327
Oh, those?

695
00:56:53,410 --> 00:56:55,370
I'm not unpacking. I'm packing.

696
00:57:01,293 --> 00:57:02,419
I'm...

697
00:57:03,086 --> 00:57:04,755
I'm going back to Canada.

698
00:57:06,715 --> 00:57:07,716
What?

699
00:57:08,717 --> 00:57:09,718
Why?

700
00:57:12,429 --> 00:57:13,680
It's just...

701
00:57:14,640 --> 00:57:17,309
hard and painful for me to see you.

702
00:57:20,270 --> 00:57:21,772
And I don't like it here anymore.

703
00:57:26,026 --> 00:57:27,694
Then what about school?

704
00:57:28,945 --> 00:57:32,157
I'm quitting. I'm done with robotics, too.

705
00:57:34,534 --> 00:57:36,745
You're going to quit school and robotics?

706
00:57:36,828 --> 00:57:38,205
Then what are you going to do?

707
00:57:40,123 --> 00:57:42,250
That, I'll have to think about
from now on.

708
00:57:46,004 --> 00:57:47,673
Are you threatening me right now?

709
00:57:48,632 --> 00:57:49,633
Threatening you?

710
00:57:51,093 --> 00:57:53,136
"I'm falling apart like this
because of you,

711
00:57:53,220 --> 00:57:55,806
so you should take responsibility."
That's what you mean.

712
00:58:01,019 --> 00:58:03,313
It is something like that, yeah.

713
00:58:09,653 --> 00:58:11,446
Do whatever you want.

714
00:58:11,530 --> 00:58:14,950
Whether you go to Canada or not,
I don't care one bit.

715
00:58:15,992 --> 00:58:16,993
Yeah.

716
00:58:17,869 --> 00:58:21,289
You've always known exactly
what you like and don't like.

717
00:58:22,207 --> 00:58:23,792
And you're stubborn, too.

718
00:58:23,875 --> 00:58:27,546
I know once you say something,
you never take it back.

719
00:58:33,969 --> 00:58:37,431
They say time heals all wounds
for a reason, you know.

720
00:58:39,933 --> 00:58:42,018
At first, you'll feel
like you're going crazy.

721
00:58:42,102 --> 00:58:44,020
You won't be able to breathe or sleep.

722
00:58:46,648 --> 00:58:50,986
But then, you'll start breathing
and sleeping again.

723
00:58:53,488 --> 00:58:57,200
You'll start craving food again,
and all that.

724
00:59:00,579 --> 00:59:04,458
Then at some point, you'll look back
and wonder, "Why was I so sad back then?"

725
00:59:06,001 --> 00:59:07,836
That day will come pretty soon.

726
00:59:18,221 --> 00:59:19,306
I'm sorry.

727
00:59:21,224 --> 00:59:22,809
I messed up.

728
00:59:24,603 --> 00:59:25,896
I don't want to hear it.

729
00:59:28,815 --> 00:59:29,941
I know.

730
00:59:30,984 --> 00:59:34,821
What I did was so wrong,
it can't be forgiven or taken back.

731
00:59:37,157 --> 00:59:39,951
You see, at first,

732
00:59:40,035 --> 00:59:43,580
I tried to think of any way
I could get you back.

733
00:59:45,874 --> 00:59:49,211
But then I realized
there's no way you'll forgive me.

734
00:59:50,545 --> 00:59:53,465
Because I can't even forgive myself,
any more than you can.

735
00:59:55,801 --> 00:59:59,805
Back then, I thought
that was the best thing I could do.

736
01:00:01,223 --> 01:00:02,974
But looking back now,

737
01:00:04,768 --> 01:00:08,605
I did all that to protect my pride.

738
01:00:11,274 --> 01:00:12,400
I know.

739
01:00:13,985 --> 01:00:16,196
I know you did that because you were sick.

740
01:00:16,279 --> 01:00:17,364
No.

741
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:23,453
I said I wanted to break up
because of you, for your sake,

742
01:00:26,081 --> 01:00:27,749
but I think that was a lie too.

743
01:00:32,838 --> 01:00:35,090
Being with you...

744
01:00:36,967 --> 01:00:38,760
made me happy.

745
01:00:39,886 --> 01:00:43,098
It made me happy,
but it also really scared me.

746
01:00:45,517 --> 01:00:47,727
I was scared that one day, it'd all end.

747
01:00:48,812 --> 01:00:50,272
And that I'd be abandoned.

748
01:00:51,106 --> 01:00:55,318
I was always holding back
because I didn't want to get hurt,

749
01:00:56,903 --> 01:00:58,780
always finding excuses to run away.

750
01:01:02,784 --> 01:01:03,785
You said...

751
01:01:05,579 --> 01:01:08,540
losing me scared you more
than dying, right?

752
01:01:10,458 --> 01:01:11,835
You said

753
01:01:13,670 --> 01:01:15,463
you thought you'd rather die.

754
01:01:25,432 --> 01:01:30,186
And I let you die
because I didn't want to get hurt.

755
01:01:31,146 --> 01:01:32,147
So...

756
01:01:34,733 --> 01:01:39,070
I'm the most selfish coward in the world.

757
01:01:45,952 --> 01:01:47,621
Who did I think I was?

758
01:01:47,704 --> 01:01:49,623
You loved me so much,

759
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:52,834
but I didn't.

760
01:01:55,253 --> 01:01:57,422
You loved me,

761
01:01:59,758 --> 01:02:01,009
but I didn't.

762
01:02:03,553 --> 01:02:04,554
No.

763
01:02:07,349 --> 01:02:08,642
You loved me.

764
01:02:10,644 --> 01:02:12,103
You loved me so much.

765
01:02:27,369 --> 01:02:29,746
Come on, I mean it.

766
01:02:32,248 --> 01:02:34,209
You have no idea how happy you made me.

767
01:02:36,002 --> 01:02:38,421
And how happy I am now.

768
01:02:41,716 --> 01:02:45,512
You have no idea how happy I am
to have you back here

769
01:02:47,263 --> 01:02:49,015
by my side, safe and sound.

770
01:02:50,934 --> 01:02:52,727
And how much I love you.

771
01:03:01,611 --> 01:03:03,029
Get up. Look at me.

772
01:03:08,076 --> 01:03:09,452
Don't you trust me?

773
01:03:10,787 --> 01:03:12,664
Have you seen me lie?

774
01:03:13,707 --> 01:03:14,749
Yeah.

775
01:04:05,592 --> 01:04:09,512
BETWEEN STEPS

776
01:04:09,596 --> 01:04:12,599
[Youjin] <i>If you thought</i>
<i>I forgave it all, you're wrong.</i>

777
01:04:12,682 --> 01:04:14,517
<i>We're not back together.</i>

778
01:04:15,226 --> 01:04:16,227
-Oh?
-[groans]

779
01:04:16,311 --> 01:04:17,937
When did you get here?

780
01:04:18,021 --> 01:04:20,940
[Youjin] <i>Thinking about me</i>
<i>before going to bed. You can do that too.</i>

781
01:04:21,024 --> 01:04:24,319
If they're Youjin's, why don't you
give them to her yourself?

782
01:04:24,402 --> 01:04:25,987
[Jihoon] <i>They're yours.</i>

783
01:04:26,071 --> 01:04:29,199
[Minjae] <i>Seriously,</i>
<i>what are you going to do if I die?</i>

784
01:04:29,282 --> 01:04:31,868
<i>Youjin, I think this is it for us.</i>

785
01:04:31,951 --> 01:04:34,537
Just like me. I said you could love me.

786
01:04:34,621 --> 01:04:36,831
[Minjae] <i>Let's end this.</i>
<i>I really want to stop doing this.</i>
